---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";
export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "Phrasal verbs · A2 Vocabulary · Curriculum Map",
  "slug": "phrasal-verbs",
  "level": "A2",
  "topic": "Phrasal verbs (common)",
  "category": "Vocabulary & Topics",
  "contentType": "vocabulary",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "In English, a verb plus a small word often makes a completely new meaning: wake up , turn off , find out . Learn each pair as one chunk , the way you learned get up in your daily r",
  "sequence": 19,
  "prerequisites": [],
  "related": [],
  "assessments": [
    "a2-exit"
  ]
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 19</p>
  <h1>Phrasal <em>verbs</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">In English, a verb plus a small word often makes a completely new meaning: <span class="ex">wake up</span>, <span class="ex">turn off</span>, <span class="ex">find out</span>. Learn each pair as <strong>one chunk</strong>, the way you learned <span class="ex">get up</span> in your daily routines lesson, and everyday English starts to sound natural: <span class="ex">I wake up at six</span>, <span class="ex">Can you pick me up at eight?</span>, <span class="ex">Please fill out this form</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">verb + small word</span>
    <span class="tag">learn whole chunks</span>
    <span class="tag">12 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Read one busy morning.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Verb + small word = new meaning.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose, type, and build chunks.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Tell your routine and give instructions.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">You already know the small words: <span class="ex">up</span>, <span class="ex">off</span>, <span class="ex">on</span>, <span class="ex">out</span>, <span class="ex">back</span>, <span class="ex">down</span>. Together with a verb, they make one new idea. Always say the two words together: <span class="ex">get up</span>, not just <span class="ex">get</span>.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="get">get</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="gets">gets</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="it">it</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="its">its</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sit">sit</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sits">sits</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="get" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> up at seven every morning. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 · daily routines · get up was already there)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I love this song. Play <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="it" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> again, please. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 · object pronouns)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Please <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sit" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> down; the meeting is starting. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 · imperatives)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Six chunks you can picture</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Say each one aloud in a sentence about you: <span class="ex">I wake up at six.</span> <span class="ex">I go out on Fridays.</span></p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/alarm-clock.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">wake up</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/tshirt.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">put on</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/laptop.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">turn on</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/phone.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">pick up</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/wastebasket.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">throw away</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/door.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">go out</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Read one busy morning</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“I wake up at six and get up at 6:15. I put on my clothes and turn on the coffee machine. At seven I go out. In the evening I come back, take off my shoes, and turn off my phone.”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Look at <span class="ex">get up</span>. You know <span class="ex">get</span> and you know <span class="ex">up</span>, but together they mean <strong>leave your bed</strong>. Does <span class="ex">get</span> alone mean that?</li>
      <li>Compare <span class="ex">turn on</span> and <span class="ex">turn off</span>. The verb is the same. Which word changes the meaning?</li>
      <li>Count the pairs of verb + small word in this little story. How many can you find?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: finish each chunk</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The verb carries the action; the small word completes the meaning. Choose the small word that finishes each chunk.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="up">up</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on">on</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="off">off</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="out">out</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="back">back</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I wake <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="up" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at six. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(stop sleeping)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I put <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> my jacket before work. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(clothes go on your body)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>She takes <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="off" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> her shoes at the door. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(remove them)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>We go <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="out" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on Friday nights. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(leave home for fun)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>He comes <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="back" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> home at seven. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(returns)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Turn <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="off" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the lights when you leave. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(stop them)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: verb + small word = one new verb</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A phrasal verb is a normal verb (<span class="ex">get, turn, put, take</span>) plus a small word (<span class="ex">up, off, on, out, back, down</span>). Together they mean something new. Don’t translate the two parts separately; learn the pair as <strong>one piece of vocabulary</strong>, exactly like a single word.</p>
  <p><strong>Morning and home.</strong> The chunks of your daily routine:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>chunk <span class="contraction">meaning</span></th><th>hear it in a sentence</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>wake up</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">stop sleeping</span></td><td>I wake up at six, but I stay in bed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>get up</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">leave your bed</span></td><td>I get up at 6:15 and make coffee.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>put on</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">place clothes on your body</span></td><td>Put on a warm jacket; it’s cold.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>take off</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">remove clothes</span></td><td>He takes off his shoes at the door.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>turn on / turn off</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">start / stop a light or machine</span></td><td>Turn on the laptop. Turn off the lights.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><strong>Out and about.</strong> Moving around the city:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>chunk <span class="contraction">meaning</span></th><th>hear it in a sentence</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>go out</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">leave home, often for fun</span></td><td>We go out for dinner on Fridays.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>come back</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">return</span></td><td>She comes back from work at six.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>get on / get off</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">enter / leave a bus or train</span></td><td>Get on the 42 bus and get off at Central Station.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>pick up</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">collect someone in a car</span></td><td>I’ll pick you up at eight.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><strong>Work and life admin.</strong> Forms, plans, and information:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>chunk <span class="contraction">meaning</span></th><th>hear it in a sentence</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>find out</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">learn a fact</span></td><td>I need to find out the schedule.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>fill out</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">complete a form</span></td><td>Please fill out this form at the desk.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>write down</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">write it so you remember</span></td><td>Write down the address before you forget it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>look for</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">try to find</span></td><td>I’m looking for my keys.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>give up</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">stop trying, stop a habit</span></td><td>He gave up sugar last month.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>throw away</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">put it in the trash</span></td><td>Throw away those old papers.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Where does the small word go?</h3>
    <p>Often you have a choice. <span class="ex">Turn off the light</span> and <span class="ex">turn the light off</span> are both correct.</p>
    <p>With a pronoun (<span class="ex">it, me, her, them</span>), there is no choice. The pronoun goes <strong>in the middle</strong>: <span class="ex">turn it off</span>, <span class="ex">pick me up</span>, <span class="ex">write them down</span>. Never <span class="ex">turn off it</span>, never <span class="ex">pick up me</span>.</p>
    <p>One chunk stays together: <span class="ex">look for</span>. Say <span class="ex">look for my keys</span>, <span class="ex">look for them</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: put the pronoun in the middle</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Pronouns like <b>it</b> and <b>me</b> go in the middle of the chunk, never after it.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="it off">it off</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="off it">off it</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="me up">me up</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="up me">up me</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="it out">it out</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="out it">out it</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The music is very loud. Please turn <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="it off" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(it = the music)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>My flight lands at ten. Can you pick <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="me up" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at the airport? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(collect me in a car)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Here’s the registration form. Fill <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="it out" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> before Friday. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(it = the form)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose the chunk</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2: choose the small word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Say the whole chunk aloud each time: <b>get up</b>, <b>put on</b>, <b>write down</b>. The cue in parentheses tells you the meaning.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="up">up</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on">on</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="off">off</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="out">out</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="back">back</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="down">down</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I get <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="up" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at seven and make breakfast. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(leave the bed)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>She put <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> her coat and left. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(clothes)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Get <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="off" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the bus at the last stop. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(leave the bus)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Can you pick me <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="up" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at eight? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(collect me in a car)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>He went <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="out" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> with friends on Saturday night. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(left home for fun)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Write <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="down" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the address before you forget it. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(on paper)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>I’m going to lunch. I’ll come <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="back" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at two. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(return)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Please fill <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="out" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> this form at the desk. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(complete it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 3: type the small word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Type <b>up</b>, <b>on</b>, <b>off</b>, <b>out</b>, <b>back</b>, or <b>down</b>. Each one is used exactly once.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>My alarm rings at six, but I don’t get <input class="answer-input" data-answer="up" aria-label="answer 1" /> until 6:30. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(leave the bed)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>It’s cold today. Put <input class="answer-input" data-answer="on" aria-label="answer 2" /> a warm jacket. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(clothes)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>I don’t know the price. I need to find <input class="answer-input" data-answer="out" aria-label="answer 3" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(learn the fact)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The movie is starting. Turn <input class="answer-input" data-answer="off" aria-label="answer 4" /> your phone. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(stop it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>She’s in Chicago this week. She comes <input class="answer-input" data-answer="back" aria-label="answer 5" /> on Sunday. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(returns)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Write <input class="answer-input" data-answer="down" aria-label="answer 6" /> the Wi-Fi password so you remember it. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(on paper)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="can you pick me up at eight">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the request</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">You need a ride to the airport at 8:00. Build the question, then say it. Where does <span class="ex">me</span> go?</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="up">up</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="can">Can</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="me">me</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="pick">pick</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="eight">eight</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">you</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="at">at</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="please fill out this form">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the instruction</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">You work at a front desk. A visitor needs to register. Build the polite instruction, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="form">form</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="please">Please</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="out">out</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="this">this</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="fill">fill</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="off it" data-fix="Please turn it off before the meeting." data-why="The pronoun it goes in the middle of the chunk: turn it off, never turn off it.">
    <h3>Drill 6: the pronoun in the wrong place</h3>
    <p>Tap the part that is wrong. Where does a pronoun live inside a chunk?</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="please">Please</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="turn">turn</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="off it">off it</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="before">before</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the">the</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="meeting">meeting.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="about" data-fix="I need to find out the schedule." data-why="The chunk is find out: two words that work as one verb. Find alone is not enough, and about does not complete it.">
    <h3>Drill 7: half a chunk</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. Which small word completes <span class="ex">find</span> when you want to learn a fact?</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="need">need</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="find">find</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="about">about</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the">the</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="schedule">schedule.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: swap the thing for a pronoun, then say it</h3>
    <p>Say the new sentence aloud with <span class="ex">it</span>, <span class="ex">her</span>, or <span class="ex">them</span> before you reveal. Remember where the pronoun goes.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> Turn off the TV. &nbsp;→&nbsp; use a pronoun</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Turn it off.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Put on your jacket. &nbsp;→&nbsp; use a pronoun</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Put it on.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> Pick up Maria at eight. &nbsp;→&nbsp; use a pronoun</p>
