  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your morning in chunks:</b> Tell the story of your morning using at least five phrasal verbs. <span class="ex">I wake up at six, get up at 6:15, put on my clothes, turn on the coffee machine, and go out at seven.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Interview the teacher:</b> Ask about their routine with phrasal verbs, then report one answer back. <span class="ex">What time do you wake up? Do you go out on weekends? When do you come back?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Give instructions:</b> You are leaving the classroom or office last. Tell the teacher what to turn on and turn off. <span class="ex">Please turn off the projector and the lights. Turn on the hallway light.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A recent form:</b> Describe a form you filled out recently: at a bank, a clinic, a delivery app. <span class="ex">Last month I filled out a form at the bank. I wrote down my address and phone number.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Something you gave up:</b> Talk about a habit you stopped, and why. <span class="ex">I gave up sugar in January. The first two weeks were hard.</span></div>

